# The lantern's reactions to things you do, said in speech bubbles beside
# him. Each section is one thing he might say, tagged with the moment it's
# for: the game says "caught" when you land a fish, and he says one of the
# caught sections (never the same one twice running, if there's another).
# See scripts/dialogue/remark.gd for the tags and guards a section can have.
#
# Moments: returned, caught, morning, table_bare, supper, dim,
# pulled_out, crab_killed.
# Placeholder writing: rewrite freely.

# (His first words, the night he pulled you from the sea, are in the opening
# cutscene: intro.dlg.)

# You've come back to a saved voyage.
~ returned_1 [on returned]
lantern: You're back. I kept the light on.

~ returned_2 [on returned]
lantern: There you are again.
lantern: I didn't go anywhere. I can't, really.

# You've landed a fish.
~ caught_1 [on caught]
lantern: A fish! Is home a fish? ...No. Probably not. [shout]

~ caught_2 [on caught]
lantern: That one looked like it knew the way.

~ caught_3 [on caught]
lantern: Supper! I'll watch. I'm very good at watching.

# You've woken at dawn.
~ morning_1 [on morning]
lantern: Morning! Did you sleep? I don't. I just glow quieter.

~ morning_2 [on morning]
lantern: The rain's tired too, I think.

~ morning_3 [on morning]
lantern: Look, it's grey and pink. That's my favourite colour.

# You've rung the galley bell for supper with nothing on the table (#207).
~ table_bare_1 [on table_bare]
lantern: Supper? ...There's nothing on the table.

~ table_bare_2 [on table_bare]
lantern: I came all this way! Well. All the way from my table.

# You've shared a meal with him.
~ supper_1 [on supper]
lantern: Oh, that's warm all the way through.

~ supper_2 [on supper]
lantern: Mm. Tastes like a Tuesday. A good one.

~ supper_3 [on supper]
lantern: I'm glowing. Am I glowing? I'm glowing.

~ supper_4 [on supper]
lantern: You cook like someone who's been missed.

# His warmth is running low.
~ dim_1 [on dim]
lantern: I'm a bit... dim. Is there soup?

~ dim_2 [on dim]
lantern: Is it me, or is it darker in here? It's me, isn't it. [thought]

# A creature has beaten you, and he's pulled you back to the landing.
~ pulled_out_1 [on pulled_out]
lantern: Got you! I've got you. You dropped some things. I didn't count.

~ pulled_out_2 [on pulled_out]
lantern: Up you come. Crabs don't fight fair. They've got far too many arms.

~ pulled_out_3 [on pulled_out]
lantern: That's twice I've pulled you out of somewhere. I'm keeping score. Kindly.

# You've killed a crab: supper.
~ crab_killed_1 [on crab_killed]
lantern: Supper! Don't forget the meat. I'd carry it, but I'd cook it. [shout]

~ crab_killed_2 [on crab_killed]
lantern: Sorry, crab. Thank you, crab. That's how the cook says it.

~ crab_killed_3 [on crab_killed]
lantern: Oh, well struck. The crew will eat well tonight.
